{"pack": "m2talk", "voice": "boy", "speaker": {"am_puck": 0.8, "af_heart": 0.2}, "audio": "m2talk-20261117.mp4", "model": "Kokoro-82M v1.0 (Apache 2.0) via kokoro-onnx (MIT); misaki phonemizer (Apache 2.0)", "gap": 0.45, "clips": {"{name}! You did it, the lighthouse shines again!": [0.0, 2.143], "Marlo's old sea chart shows a big city across the sea. It's Port Lumen!": [2.593, 4.959], "And the Crumb Crew went that way!": [8.001, 1.78], "My new boat, the Sea Sprout, is ready for long trips. But look at the sea: the tide is going out!": [10.231, 5.983], "At low tide, a sand path goes from this old dock to Port Lumen.": [16.664, 4.063], "It's the Tidewalk. Walk it! Juniper is coming too.": [21.177, 2.953], "Port Lumen? Walk the Tidewalk, {name}! It starts at the old dock, east of the lighthouse.": [24.58, 4.895], "The Sea Sprout is for long trips, far away. Someday!": [29.925, 3.508], "Mo's boat, the Sea Sprout, is finished. It's waiting at the harbor.": [33.883, 3.828], "Wow, {name}! We walked all the way across the sea! Look at this city: canals, bridges, so many houses!": [38.161, 6.068], "This is Port Lumen. The Tidewalk will take us home whenever we like, from this beach.": [44.679, 5.065], "Barney said the crew sold a page at the market here. Let\u2019s find it! Look, people are waiting for us!": [50.194, 6.068], "So many streets! Good thing you know how to read a map.": [56.712, 2.932], "People are waiting on the pier. Market Street is just up the road. The Town Hall is north, past the big canal.": [60.094, 7.135], "The Sea Sprout is resting, {name}.": [67.679, 1.673], "To go home to Lighthouse Island, walk the Tidewalk from the Old Town beach!": [69.802, 4.532], "\"Welcome to Port Lumen, the city of canals!\"": [74.784, 2.761], "\"Water taxis stop at the yellow signs.\"": [77.995, 2.463], "The big clock on the tower has stopped.": [80.908, 2.079], "Its hands point to ten past three: the time the storm hit.": [83.437, 3.636], "A statue of the person who started the city long ago.": [87.523, 3.231], "The plaque is covered in mud from the storm. You can't read it yet.": [91.203, 3.871], "An old stone well in the Old Town square. Coins sparkle at the bottom.": [95.524, 4.532], "People make a wish when they drop one in.": [100.506, 2.335], "A water taxi stop.": [103.291, 1.524], "Welcome to Port Lumen! I'm Mayor Bea.": [105.265, 2.441], "Since the storm, our big clock has stopped. Nobody knows what time it is!": [108.156, 4.553], "The water taxis are late, the market opens whenever it wants\u2026 what a mess!": [113.159, 4.511], "And someone came to the market selling old pages with maps on them. Very strange!": [118.12, 5.321], "And this is Gus, our clockmaker. He came to meet you!": [123.891, 3.06], "Tick\u2026 tock\u2026 no, nothing. Hello there! I'm Gus, the clockmaker.": [127.401, 3.615], "The night of the storm, my tower shook and some gears slipped. The hands are stuck at ten past three.": [131.466, 6.025], "Help the people of Port Lumen and learn all you can!": [137.941, 3.081], "Take this road to Market Street. Start at Ms. Reyes\u2019s book stall. Go stall by stall to Rafi\u2019s fish market.": [141.473, 6.836], "Then come to my Clock Tower!": [148.759, 1.737], "Huge gears, as big as wagon wheels. They're stuck.": [150.946, 3.103], "Some gears slipped out of place. Gus will need help putting them back.": [154.499, 3.913], "A model of an old sailing ship.": [158.862, 1.972], "A card says it brought the first families to Port Lumen long ago.": [161.284, 3.828], "An empty display case. The card says: \"An old map of the sea\".": [165.562, 4.02], "The map is gone!": [170.032, 1.225], "Today's flavors: vanilla, strawberry, chocolate, mint, mango and blueberry.": [171.707, 4.575], "The ships board: when each boat comes and goes.": [176.732, 2.783], "Every time says \"???\" \u2014 the clock tower stopped, so nobody knows the time!": [179.965, 4.383], "A big map of Port Lumen on the wall.": [184.797, 2.121], "Three canals cross the city. They are the Grand Canal, the North Canal and the Harbor Canal.": [187.369, 5.556], "Old photos of the city long ago. The Town Hall looks almost the same!": [193.375, 4.489], "But there were no water taxis back then: people rowed little boats.": [198.314, 3.892], "Fresh fish! Fresh fish! Hello, I'm Rafi.": [202.656, 2.548], "The storm brought lots of seaweed into the harbor. The fish love it!": [205.654, 3.977], "Hello! I'm Ms. Patel. I teach violin.": [210.081, 2.527], "Every evening I play by my window. Since the clock stopped, I never know when to start!": [213.058, 5.321], "Hi there. I'm Mr. Diaz. I grow vegetables on my roof!": [218.829, 3.764], "The storm blew my tomatoes all over the Old Town. Ha!": [223.043, 3.849], "Hey! I'm Ruby! Want to see me skate? Watch\u2026 whoa!": [227.343, 3.039], "Those pirates ran past me yesterday. One of them was a little bird with a blue feather!": [230.831, 5.471], "Good day, dear. I'm Mrs. Chen. I knit hats and scarves for the whole street.": [236.752, 4.681], "When it gets cold, come and see me.": [241.883, 2.1], "Hi! I'm Leo. I bring the mail on my bike.": [244.433, 2.719], "I ride so fast I'm never late\u2026 but with no clock, I don't know if I'm early!": [247.602, 4.895], "Ah, a new face. I'm Grandpa Walt. Do you play chess?": [252.947, 3.273], "I've lived in the Old Town for seventy years. I remember when the clock was built.": [256.67, 4.852], "Hi! I'm Nora. I run around the park every morning.": [261.972, 3.337], "Did you see the ducks on the pond? They're the best runners\u2026 swimmers!": [265.759, 3.721], "Flowers! Lovely flowers! I'm Mr. Bloom.": [269.931, 2.548], "A flower for every friend. Every friend for a flower!": [272.929, 3.252], "Hi! I'm Hana. I fly kites in the park.": [276.631, 2.655], "From up high, my kite sees the whole city, like a map!": [279.735, 3.188], "Hello, explorer! I'm Officer Dale. I help keep Port Lumen safe.": [283.373, 4.105], "If you see those pirates, tell me. But be careful!": [287.929, 2.847], "A violin and a music stand. The notes say: \"Evening song\".": [291.225, 3.743], "Pots of tomatoes, peppers and beans, ready for the roof garden.": [295.418, 3.935], "A red skateboard covered in stickers.": [299.803, 2.249], "Balls of yarn and two knitting needles. A scarf is almost done.": [302.502, 4.127], "A mail bike with a big basket.": [307.079, 1.929], "A chess board in the middle of a game. Whose turn is it?": [309.458, 3.167], "Running shoes, a little muddy from the park.": [313.075, 2.42], "Buckets of fresh flowers for tomorrow's market.": [315.945, 2.74], "A blue kite with a long red tail.": [319.135, 2.036], "A shiny badge and a whistle on a hook.": [321.621, 2.121], "Hey, I'm Omar. I play guitar on the bridges.": [324.192, 2.889], "The canals make the music sound bigger. Listen!": [327.531, 2.996], "Hi! I'm Lucy, and I build robots!": [330.977, 2.207], "My newest robot can sweep the street. Well\u2026 almost. It mostly spins in circles.": [333.634, 5.492], "Hello, mijo! I'm Mrs. Rivera. I bake cookies for the whole street.": [339.576, 4.255], "Without the clock, I never know when they're ready. I just follow my nose!": [344.281, 4.191], "Smile! Click! I'm Mr. Novak, the photographer.": [348.921, 2.911], "I take a photo of the Town Hall every year. One day, my photos will go in the museum!": [352.282, 5.577], "Hi! I'm Tia! I'm the best goalie on my team!": [358.309, 2.804], "Want to play? Oh, you're on a mission. Okay, next time!": [361.563, 3.209], "Oh, hello, dear. I'm Granny Fern. I've read every book in the City Library!": [365.223, 4.575], "Well, almost every book. The library opened again after the repairs. I go every day!": [370.247, 5.513], "Hi! I'm Kenji. I take care of my fish, Bubbles and Squirt.": [376.211, 3.721], "I come to the canal to look at the wild fish. They're faster than mine!": [380.382, 4.233], "Hi, I'm Zoe! I paint the city from the roofs.": [385.065, 2.697], "Yesterday I painted three pirates running down Market Street. Strange, right?": [388.213, 4.98], "A guitar with colorful stickers. One string is new.": [393.643, 3.337], "A little robot with a broom for an arm. It beeps!": [397.43, 3.039], "A plate of warm cookies. They smell like cinnamon!": [400.919, 2.932], "An old camera and a box of photos of the Town Hall.": [404.301, 3.188], "A shiny trophy and a ball.": [407.939, 1.716], "A tall pile of library books, all read twice.": [410.105, 2.889], "A fishbowl with two orange fish: Bubbles and Squirt.": [413.444, 3.295], "A painting of the canals at sunset. The paint is still wet!": [417.189, 3.593], "Welcome to Sip & Snack! I'm Kiki!": [421.232, 2.249], "The storm broke the Galleria's glass roof. The workers fixed it yesterday, so we're open again!": [423.931, 5.812], "Oh, but there's a problem. My berry smoothies need fresh mint, and I don't have any left.": [430.193, 5.3], "Olive grows mint in the greenhouse, in City Park. Could you ask her for some, {name}?": [435.943, 4.553], "Meanwhile, take a look at what I have!": [440.947, 2.185], "Olive's greenhouse is in City Park, by the pond. She has the best mint in town!": [443.582, 5.3], "Want something while you wait?": [449.332, 1.567], "Is that... fresh mint? It smells amazing!": [451.349, 2.676], "Now I can make smoothies again! The first one is for you, {name}.": [454.475, 3.316], "And here are some shells. Thank you, explorer!": [458.241, 2.569], "Hi again, {name}! What would you like?": [461.26, 1.609], "Good day! I am Mr. Fitz, and I make hats.": [463.319, 2.569], "A good hat keeps the sun out of your eyes. And it makes you feel brave!": [466.339, 4.127], "I made every hat in this shop with my own two hands. Have a look!": [470.915, 3.956], "Ah, my favorite customer! Looking for a new hat?": [475.321, 2.868], "Hey hey! Welcome to Funhouse Toys! I'm Pepper!": [478.639, 2.783], "Kites, yo-yos, boats... Toys don't run out. You can play with them again and again!": [481.872, 4.767], "Back for more fun? Let's see!": [487.089, 1.78], "A fountain under the new glass roof. The water sparkles in the sunlight.": [489.319, 4.425], "Some people make a wish here. What would you wish for?": [494.194, 2.868], "THE GALLERIA: Sip & Snack, Topper Hats, Funhouse Toys.": [497.512, 3.444], "At the bottom it says: \"More shops coming soon!\"": [501.406, 2.932], "Welcome to my library, {name}! I\u2019m Ms. Reyes. The books are back on their shelves.": [504.788, 4.297], "We just opened again after the storm. Most of our books are dry, thank goodness.": [509.535, 5.108], "But one book never came back. Dr. Kai, at the aquarium, borrowed it a long time ago.": [515.093, 5.492], "Could you ask him for it, {name}? Books are happiest on their shelves.": [521.035, 3.252], "The aquarium is right next door, on the east side. Dr. Kai is always busy with his fish!": [524.737, 5.727], "My book! You found it!": [530.914, 1.396], "Thank you, {name}. A library is a place where everyone shares, and that means bringing books back.": [532.76, 5.321], "Here are some shells, for a very helpful reader.": [538.531, 2.761], "Every Saturday I read stories on the rug. You're always welcome, {name}.": [541.743, 3.956], "A soft rug with cushions, for story time.": [546.149, 2.612], "A little sign says: \"Quiet voices, big ideas.\"": [549.211, 3.188], "Big old books: \"Records of Port Lumen.\"": [552.849, 2.505], "Some pages are missing. Maybe somebody in town knows where they are...": [555.804, 4.361], "Welcome to the City Aquarium! I'm Dr. Kai. I take care of all the fish here.": [560.615, 4.831], "Every fish in these tanks is a real fish. They all live in the water around us.": [565.896, 4.767], "Go close to a tank and press A. You can read all about the fish inside!": [571.113, 4.404], "Catch one of these fish in the wild! Then it goes in your field journal. Watching here doesn't count!": [575.967, 5.94], "A library book? Oh no... I forgot all about it!": [582.357, 3.017], "It was under my fish food. Please take it back to Ms. Reyes, and tell her I'm sorry.": [585.824, 5.151], "A tank full of water and plants.": [591.425, 1.887], "Oh! A visitor! Welcome to my greenhouse. I'm Olive.": [593.761, 2.953], "The storm broke three glass panes. Now they're fixed, and my plants are warm again.": [597.165, 5.065], "Here, have a fruit cup. Fresh and sweet!": [602.68, 2.484], "Mint for Kiki? Of course! I have plenty.": [605.614, 2.591], "Here you go. Tell her to save me a smoothie!": [608.655, 2.505], "The bees visit my flowers every day. Go look at the bee box, but don't bother them!": [611.61, 5.044], "Olive's tomato plants climb up tall wooden poles. Some tomatoes are already red!": [617.104, 5.577], "Mint for Kiki? Of course! I have plenty. Here you go.": [623.131, 3.188], "And a fruit cup for you, fresh and sweet. Tell Kiki to save me a smoothie!": [626.769, 4.383], "TREASURE! An old pocket watch, half-buried in the sand!": [631.602, 3.06], "Its hands don't move anymore. It looks very, very old.": [635.112, 3.444], "A letter in a bottle, with a little anchor drawn on it.": [639.006, 2.953], "\"Hello! I'm Ana. I sail a small cargo boat between the islands.\"": [642.409, 4.361], "\"When I come to Port Lumen, I listen for the big clock. This time it was quiet. I hope it gets fixed! \u2014 Ana\"": [647.221, 7.028], "Thank you for helping Gus. Now, a mayor has to think about the past, too.": [654.699, 4.468], "Why did our city do the things it did? Let's think like historians!": [659.617, 3.999], "\u00a1Hola! I'm Pedro, captain of the water taxis!": [664.065, 2.825], "Stand by any yellow sign and press A, and I'll take you anywhere. But first, can you read my canal map?": [667.341, 6.452], "Ahoy! I'm Captain Lin, the harbor master. I know every ship that comes and goes.": [674.243, 5.044], "Three pirates sailed in on a leaky old ship. The Leaky Biscuit, it was called!": [679.737, 4.767], "But my harbor isn't only for pirates. Let me show you what moves through it every day.": [684.953, 5.172], "I sell so many fish that I count them in crates and boxes. Want to learn my trick?": [690.575, 5.129], "Hi hi! I\u2019m Coco! I make the best ice cream in Port Lumen!": [696.155, 3.977], "My freezer stopped in the storm and some ice cream melted. Is it ruined forever? Let's find out!": [700.582, 5.94], "Hey, it's you again! I need help with my sales chart before I order new toys.": [706.972, 4.809], "Bars, numbers\u2026 it's like a game! Ready?": [712.231, 2.313], "Ah, you're back! Can you say what a hat is like, with just the right words?": [714.995, 3.764], "A hat maker needs good words for his signs. Let me teach you.": [719.209, 3.764], "My visitors always ask me questions they could answer themselves\u2026 if they knew how to read a fact page!": [723.423, 6.388], "A fact page tells true things that you can check.": [730.261, 2.783], "Let me show you the secret helpers on every page.": [733.493, 3.039], "Would you like to learn another reader\u2019s trick?": [736.982, 2.185], "Some long words are just two small words holding hands!": [739.617, 3.401], "Hello! I\u2019m Dr. Amara. I take care of the old treasures in the City Museum.": [743.469, 4.937], "Something old and important is missing from my museum: an old sea map! The storm? Or\u2026 someone sneaky?": [748.856, 6.815], "To solve mysteries of the past, we need good questions. Let me show you.": [756.121, 4.425], "Want to see how a real scientist finds things out? My plants are perfect for a test!": [760.996, 5.364], "You came from the island? I grew up on a farm, far from any city. Life there is very different!": [766.81, 5.94], "Want to see my favorite inventor's secret? It's all about pieces!": [773.2, 4.041], "I've lived in the Old Town for seventy years. People thought very differently back then! Sit, I'll tell you.": [777.691, 6.239], "Gears, gears, gears\u2026 When everyone in town has helped, we'll make this clock tick again!": [784.38, 4.767], "Port Lumen is lucky to have you, {name}. Keep asking why!": [789.597, 3.145], "Have you heard of the Castle League?": [793.192, 1.844], "Explorers with all ten medals go to a big castle. Five champions wait there!": [795.486, 5.193], "Need a ride? Stand by any yellow taxi sign and press A!": [801.129, 3.572], "Ships in, ships out. Goods, people and news, all day long!": [805.151, 3.849], "My new freezer works! The melted ice cream froze again. Come back for a scoop!": [809.451, 4.703], "Who? What? When? Why? Keep asking, and the past will answer!": [814.603, 3.231], "You helped the city, {name}, and you\u2019re Canal Cup champion! You know the number line and how pieces fit. Go!": [818.284, 6.153], "Let's fix the big clock together. First the gears, then the time!": [824.887, 3.828], "It's working! Listen\u2026 five more minutes to midnight\u2026": [829.165, 2.975], "DONG! DONG! DONG! The bells are ringing again!": [832.59, 2.569], "Wait. Did you hear that? Someone up there shouted: \"MY EARS!\"": [835.609, 3.38], "Nobody should be above the bells. Take the ladder, {name}. I'll be right behind you!": [839.439, 4.233], "The ladder goes up to the old room above the bells. Go on, I'm right behind you!": [844.123, 4.959], "Tick, tock! My clock has never worked better. Thank you, {name}!": [849.531, 3.081], "The gears turn smoothly now. Tick, tock, tick, tock.": [853.063, 3.316], "Shh! Who's there?! Oh, it's YOU. All right, all right, you found us!": [856.829, 4.169], "I'm Captain Rascal Crumb. We hid up here to read the museum's old sea map in secret.": [861.448, 5.535], "It has an X on it. We thought the treasure was in Port Lumen\u2026 but we dug everywhere and found nothing!": [867.433, 5.94], "Hmph. You think you're so clever? BRIOCHE! Our navigator knows every number in this city. Show this explorer!": [873.823, 7.497], "You\u2026 I didn't think I'd see you again.": [881.77, 1.972], "Doesn't matter! The Crumb Crew is my crew now. Let's see what you've got!": [884.192, 3.892], "Why did you leave him in the storm?. We're not scared of you!.": [888.534, 2.975], "No more talking. Round one!": [891.959, 1.801], "Arr\u2026 you really ARE clever.": [894.21, 1.481], "Fine. Here's the museum's map. And that glowing page? We traded it for a bag of cookies. Yum!": [896.141, 6.089], "The X isn't here anyway. Look: it's on an island far to the south. We'll find it first! Come on, crew!": [902.681, 6.089], "(Pip winks at you before flying after the ship.)": [909.22, 2.719], "Oh! Hello again, little explorer! I'm Barney, the cook.": [912.389, 3.124], "Captain says we're on a treasure hunt. I just want a quiet kitchen\u2026": [915.963, 3.956], "Psst! Squawk! It was me! I left the parrot clues all over town.": [920.369, 3.785], "I wanted somebody to find us. The captain isn't bad, just\u2026 a little greedy. Pieces of eight!": [924.604, 5.705], "Three big bells, still shaking after midnight. Hmmm-mmm-mmm\u2026": [930.759, 4.084], "A note in big messy letters: \"See you on the next island, little explorer! \u2014 Captain Crumb\"": [935.293, 5.535], "The old sea map is back in its case. The X is far to the south\u2026": [941.278, 4.191], "The sea map is back where it belongs! Thank you, {name}.": [945.919, 2.697], "Look at that X\u2026 on an island far to the south. I wonder what's there.": [949.066, 3.956], "The big clock is ticking again. Everyone in Port Lumen knows the time now!": [953.472, 4.468], "{name}, you saved Port Lumen! You\u2019ve done so well\u2026 I have something for you.": [958.39, 3.913], "Look at the end of the pier: a little boat, just your size! I fixed her up myself. She\u2019s yours!": [962.753, 5.791], "The X on the old sea map is on Rootwood Island. It's far to the southeast.": [968.994, 4.681], "Sail the Sea Lane and you\u2019ll find it!": [974.125, 2.015], "Steer her just like walking. I\u2019ll follow you in the Sea Sprout.": [976.59, 3.572], "Would you like to learn to read a clock to five minutes? It\u2019s a clockmaker\u2019s favorite skill.": [980.612, 5.108], "Yes, please!. Maybe later.": [986.17, 1.652], "Your boat is tied at the end of the pier, {name}. Sail east along the Sea Lane to Rootwood Island!": [988.272, 5.599], "I'm Ruby! The storm smashed the little dock at this taxi stop. The water taxi can't stop here!": [994.321, 5.855], "Rafi has planks at the fish market. Learn with the people of Market Street first, then come back!": [1000.625, 5.961], "You learned with all of Market Street! Now we can rebuild the dock.": [1007.037, 3.785], "Then the water taxi can stop at the Harbor again, and everyone can ride!": [1011.272, 4.276], "First, a quick review. Every right answer gets you one plank. Then you build! Ready?": [1015.998, 4.959], "You have the planks! Stand by the taxi stop and press A to lay each one.": [1021.407, 4.169], "I count my skateboard tricks in tens. Today: 3 tens and 4 ones! Our dock is the best place to practice.": [1026.026, 7.327], "Five planks, and the dock is as good as new! Here comes the water taxi! YOU built it, {name}!": [1033.803, 5.023], "Let's tell Mayor Bea!": [1039.275, 1.375], "The taxi stop's dock is broken. With planks, you could lay a new one along the canal.": [1041.1, 5.343], "A water-taxi stop\u2026 but its little dock is broken. The taxi can't stop here.": [1046.893, 4.98], "Ruby is looking at it, nearby.": [1052.323, 1.887], "Hi! I'm Leo. I bring the mail on my bike\u2026 but with no clock, I never know if I'm late!": [1054.659, 5.449], "Gus says the storm knocked gears loose in the Clock Tower. Learn with the Canal Walk people first!": [1060.559, 6.089], "You learned with the whole Canal Walk! Gus found five loose gears in the tower.": [1067.098, 4.681], "They go back between the clock face and the big wheels. Gus needs our help!": [1072.229, 4.425], "A quick review first. Every right answer gets you one gear. Then you put them back! Ready?": [1077.105, 5.236], "You have the gears! Go into the Clock Tower. Press A by the big wheels to put each one back.": [1082.791, 5.193], "Five gears, all back in place. Now I just need the bells to tell me the time!": [1088.434, 4.831], "All five gears back in place! You have good hands, {name}.": [1093.715, 3.039], "Now let's turn the big wheel and\u2026 hmm. Wait a moment.": [1097.203, 3.081], "The big wheels of the clock. The five loose gears go back between them and the clock face.": [1100.735, 5.172], "The gears are back in place. But the clock still needs its Bell Gear.": [1106.357, 3.913], "{name}! Listen\u2026 footsteps, ABOVE the bells! And someone said \"shh!\"": [1110.72, 4.041], "Nobody should be up there. I put my old ladder up to the trapdoor. Go and see who it is!": [1115.211, 5.193], "The Bell Gear! Brioche gave it back. Let me put it in\u2026 there!": [1120.855, 3.444], "Tick, tock, tick, tock\u2026 the big clock is working again!": [1124.749, 3.252], "DONG! DONG! DONG! The midnight bells ring all over Port Lumen!": [1128.451, 3.807], "Oh, a visitor! I'm Mei's grandma. Mei's out in the city, but I'm always here with my yarn.": [1132.707, 5.556], "Every winter I knit one hat for each child on our street. I made one too many this year\u2026": [1138.713, 5.535], "It's yours! Keep your ears warm on the boat.": [1144.698, 2.527], "(You got the Wool Beanie! Wear it from your backpack.)": [1147.675, 2.719], "Knit one, purl one\u2026 Counting stitches is good math practice, you know!": [1150.843, 4.319], "I'm Max! Hana's at the park with her kite. I'm watching the bees from our window.": [1155.612, 4.596], "Did you know? Bumble bees can see ultraviolet light. That's a color people can't see!": [1160.658, 5.151], "So flowers look different to a bee! Here, have my shells. Look for bumble bees by day, in the park flowers!": [1166.259, 6.687], "(You got 10 shells!)": [1173.395, 1.375], "Bzzz! I want to be a bee scientist when I grow up.": [1175.22, 3.743], "Hi! I'm Omar's sister, Layla. He plays guitar all day\u2026 I fish the canals!": [1179.413, 4.895], "Want a secret? The largemouth bass hides in the calm canal water, by plants and logs.": [1184.757, 5.492], "It's most active at dawn and dusk. So fish when the sun is low!": [1190.699, 4.041], "And look at its mouth: the jaw reaches back past its eye. That's how it got its name!": [1195.191, 5.108], "(Tip: the largemouth bass bites in the city canals at dawn and dusk.)": [1200.749, 4.148], "Dawn and dusk, remember! That's bass time.": [1205.347, 2.569], "Welcome! I'm Kenji's dad. I fish in the harbor every morning.": [1208.366, 3.913], "Out at sea, Atlantic herring swim together in big schools. One female can lay 30,000 to 200,000 eggs!": [1212.729, 10.143], "That's a LOT of little fish. Here, take my spare hat. Every fisher needs one!": [1223.322, 5.108], "(You got the Yellow Bucket Hat! Wear it from your backpack.)": [1228.88, 3.209], "Kenji named his fish Bubbles and Squirt. He says Bubbles is the boss of the house!": [1232.539, 5.044], "{name}! Did you see that glow in the sea, by the lighthouse?": [1238.033, 2.612], "Go and see it first, by the rocks! Then come back, and we can talk about a trip.": [1241.095, 4.724], "Hello, mijo! Are you the explorer with the Atlas? Then I have something for you.": [1246.269, 4.681], "A raccoon in a big hat gave me this glowing paper\u2026 for a big bag of my cookies!": [1251.401, 5.044], "It hums when you come near. I think it wants to go home. Here, it's yours!": [1256.895, 4.255], "Is the page happy in its book now? Here, have a look at my cookies, mijo!": [1261.599, 4.447], "{name}! You built that dock all by yourself. You are doing so well!": [1266.496, 3.551], "Our trip is long. There are many places to see, and lots and lots of walking.": [1270.497, 4.681], "So I brought you a present. Close your eyes\u2026 Open them!": [1275.628, 3.167], "Juniper rolls out a red bike with a big basket. Your otter jumps right into it and waves!": [1279.245, 5.705], "It's yours! Open your backpack and tap Ride. When you go into a house, you get off by yourself.": [1285.4, 5.513], "Ring the bell and go, explorer!": [1291.363, 1.887], "Those three pirates bought fish and paid with\u2026 cookie crumbs! One had a green parrot on his shoulder.": [1293.7, 5.897], "You learned so much! Now help me count my crates. Then find Ruby by the broken taxi dock at the Harbor.": [1300.047, 6.537], "Here\u2019s something odd. A book about old sea maps was borrowed last week. The card is signed \"C. Crumb\".": [1307.035, 6.708], "Want to learn more? Go and see Lucy, at her robot stall on Market Street.": [1314.193, 4.532], "My robot recorded sounds at the market this morning: three voices\u2026 and a parrot saying \"Pieces of eight!\"": [1319.175, 6.473], "Want to learn more? Go and see Dr. Amara, at her stall on Market Street.": [1326.098, 4.596], "This morning a raccoon in a big hat had a stall by mine. He sold glowing paper\u2026 and packed up fast!": [1331.144, 6.559], "Want to learn more? Go and see Rafi, at the fish market by the harbor.": [1338.153, 4.169], "The thief left tiny paw prints in the dust of the empty case. Raccoon paws, I think. And a cookie crumb!": [1342.772, 6.879], "Want to learn more? Go and see Mr. Bloom, at his flower stall on Market Street.": [1350.101, 4.575], "Strange thing, amigo! The night the clock stopped, I heard a big CLANK in the Clock Tower. Then silence.": [1355.125, 6.303], "Want to learn more? Go and see Rafi, at his fish stall on the Canal Walk.": [1361.878, 4.319], "One more thing! A pirate, an otter in a navigator\u2019s cap, dropped a big shiny gear. He grabbed it and ran!": [1366.647, 6.708], "Want to learn more? Go and see Ms. Reyes, reading by the canal on the Canal Walk.": [1373.805, 4.809], "A clock book is missing: \"How Clocks Ring\". The card says\u2026 \"C. Crumb\". Again!": [1379.064, 4.745], "Want to learn more? Go and see Lucy, with her robot on the Canal Walk.": [1384.259, 4.34], "A clock is many pieces working together. If ONE gear is missing, it stops. No Bell Gear, no bells\u2026": [1389.049, 6.644], "Want to learn more? Go and see Grandpa Walt, at the west end of the Canal Walk.": [1396.143, 4.617], "When I was a boy, the midnight bells were SO loud. They\u2019d scare anyone hiding near. Did someone stop them?": [1401.211, 6.345], "Great job again! Now help Pedro with taxi riders, then find Leo by the Clock Tower. He needs you!": [1408.006, 6.431], "One more thing\u2026 Last night I heard footsteps above the bells. Nobody goes up there!": [1414.887, 5.065], "Want to learn more? Go and see Coco, by the Clock Tower on Museum Road.": [1420.402, 4.447], "A big fellow bought my warmest hat. He said: \"It\u2019s so windy up by the bells!\" Then he ran off.": [1425.299, 6.025], "Gus heard strange noises up by the bells. Go and see him in the Clock Tower!": [1431.774, 4.937], "Every night some ice cream disappears. And there are sticky footprints going toward the Clock Tower!": [1437.161, 5.641], "Want to learn more? Go and see Captain Lin, on Museum Road.": [1443.253, 3.593], "The Leaky Biscuit is still tied at the east docks. But nobody\u2019s aboard. Where did they go?": [1447.296, 5.513], "Want to learn more? Go and see Dr. Amara, in the Museum.": [1453.259, 3.679], "One more account for you: an old guard\u2019s diary. It says there is a secret room above the clock\u2019s bells!": [1457.388, 6.303], "Want to learn more? Go and see Mr. Fitz, on Museum Road.": [1464.141, 3.508], "Guess what? A green parrot bought a toy telescope. It paid with an old gold coin. A parrot! With money!": [1468.099, 6.58], "Look at my map of the harbor floor. Someone drew an X on it in pencil. What are they looking for?": [1475.129, 5.727], "Someone dug holes in my greenhouse last night! They dropped a torn corner of a map. It says: \"\u2026the X\u2026\"": [1481.305, 6.452], "Oh! I remember now. The pirates sold one page at the market. It had a map of the sea, and a nibbled corner!": [1488.207, 6.751], "A big fellow tried on every hat in my shop. He said: \"Captain Crumb needs a new one!\" Then he ran off.": [1495.408, 6.473], "Did you know? The first big clocks had no minute hand at all. People only needed the hour!": [1502.331, 5.471], "Back again, {name}? Business is booming! Boats bring fish, people buy fish\u2026": [1508.252, 4.105], "Watch how fast I add and take away my boxes!": [1512.807, 2.953], "Hello! I\u2019m Ms. Reyes, the librarian. Today my books came out to the market! Books are full of new words.": [1516.211, 6.345], "Don\u2019t know a word? The words around it are clues. Let me show you!": [1523.006, 3.657], "Hi! I\u2019m Lucy, and I build robots!": [1527.113, 2.207], "Every robot starts with choosing the right materials. Want to help me test some?": [1529.77, 4.767], "Before we fix the big clock, you need to think like a clockmaker.": [1534.987, 3.785], "Clock hands jump around a circle, numbers jump along a line. Let me show you!": [1539.222, 4.895], "Good day! I\u2019m Mr. Fitz, the hat maker. See my signs: \"unhappy hat\", \"rewrap the box\"\u2026 so many tricky words.": [1544.567, 6.985], "Little word starts can change a word\u2019s meaning. Let me teach you two!": [1552.002, 4.105], "I found something in the museum basement: two old stories of the same day!": [1556.557, 4.575], "Each one tells what one person saw. Historians compare them. Shall we look together?": [1561.582, 5.236], "You\u2019re doing so much for our city, {name}! Have you heard of the Canal Cup?": [1567.268, 3.764], "A friendly quiz on numbers and all you learn in our city. Three young players want to play: Ruby, Leo, Zoe.": [1571.482, 7.007], "Beat each one to get a badge: Canal, Bridge, and Bell. The city champion rings the big bells with Gus!": [1578.939, 6.324], "Ruby is waiting right outside, on the Town Hall Plaza. Good luck!": [1585.713, 4.233], "Hi! I\u2019m Ruby. My Canal Cup match is all about hundreds, tens, and ones.": [1590.396, 4.831], "Rafi at the fish market can teach you. Learn it, then come back!": [1595.677, 3.7], "Hi! I\u2019m Ruby. Have you met Mayor Bea? She runs the Canal Cup!": [1599.827, 3.764], "I\u2019m Ruby! I count my skateboard tricks in tens.": [1604.041, 2.996], "Yes, let\u2019s go!. Not now.": [1607.487, 1.631], "Rematch? I\u2019ve been practicing my tens!": [1609.567, 2.292], "Wow, you\u2019re fast! Here, the Canal Badge is yours.": [1612.309, 2.761], "You won the Canal Badge!": [1615.521, 1.503], "Mayor Bea will want to hear the news. Go and see her in the Town Hall!": [1617.473, 3.977], "I\u2019m Leo! My match has adding and taking away with big numbers, and questions about what you learned.": [1621.901, 5.791], "Rafi knows a trick for that. Learn it first \u2014 then I\u2019ll race you!": [1628.141, 3.743], "I\u2019m Leo! I add up my bike rides every day.": [1632.334, 2.911], "Another race? This time I\u2019m ready!": [1635.695, 2.143], "You beat me! Nobody ever beats me at big numbers\u2026 until now!": [1638.287, 3.935], "You won the Bridge Badge!": [1642.672, 1.46], "One more match to go: Zoe will be ready in the next chapter.": [1644.582, 3.615], "I\u2019m Zoe. My match is the hardest one: big numbers, story problems AND questions about everything you learned!": [1648.647, 7.156], "Learn all you can in the city first. Then come and find me!": [1656.253, 3.465], "I\u2019m Zoe. I paint numbers on my pictures\u2026 and I solve story problems for fun.": [1660.168, 5.3], "Last match of the Canal Cup! First to 5 points. Ready?": [1665.918, 3.615], "A rematch? Sure! I love story problems.": [1669.983, 2.548], "You did it! You\u2019re the Canal Cup champion!": [1672.981, 2.335], "You won the Bell Badge! You are the Canal Cup champion!": [1675.765, 3.145], "Now go and see Gus in the Clock Tower. The champion rings the big bells!": [1679.361, 4.703], "QUIZ NIGHT at the Town Hall! The whole city is here.": [1684.513, 3.06], "Big news, {name}! A raccoon in a big hat came to the market this morning\u2026 and sold a glowing page!": [1688.023, 5.492], "With a big cook and a green parrot. It\u2019s them: the Crumb Crew! They sold one page and ran off.": [1693.965, 5.769], "They traded it to Mrs. Rivera, our cookie baker. Her cookie cart is right outside, on the plaza!": [1700.185, 6.217], "A blue feather floats down from the Town Hall roof\u2026": [1706.852, 2.868], "Now we know WHO sells the pages, and our taxi dock is fixed! But why is our clock still stopped?": [1710.17, 6.132], "I found out why the clock still won't run, {name}! All the loose gears are back\u2026 but look:": [1716.752, 4.575], "The Bell Gear isn't loose. It's GONE! Someone took it, so the bells can't ring at midnight.": [1721.777, 5.044], "Somebody wanted the bells quiet\u2026 But who is hiding near those bells? Let's find out!": [1727.271, 5.087], "A big boat came in! Now I have boxes of ten and single fish everywhere.": [1732.807, 4.873], "Will you help me count them? Tens and ones!": [1738.131, 2.399], "All counted! You\u2019re a real fish-market helper, {name}.": [1740.979, 2.761], "Let me show him a trick. I toss a shell in\u2026 and he brings it back!": [1744.191, 3.721], "Amigo! My water taxis are full today. People get on, people get off\u2026": [1748.362, 4.596], "Help me count my riders? Adding and taking away to 100!": [1753.408, 3.892], "\u00a1Perfecto! Every rider counted. Thank you, {name}!": [1757.75, 2.591], "Oof! You know your tens and ones better than any navigator, {name}!": [1760.791, 3.359], "Fine, fine\u2026 here's the Bell Gear. I took it so the bells wouldn't wake us. Gus can have it back!": [1764.599, 5.833], "I\u2019m Brioche, the navigator. I know every canal\u2026 and every number in Port Lumen!": [1770.883, 5.129], "Dr. Kai comes running from the aquarium.": [1776.462, 2.548], "A Lanternhorse! I have waited my whole life to see one!": [1779.46, 3.337], "It\u2019s a magic creature of Otterpage, not a real animal. Real seahorses live in the sea, and they don\u2019t glow.": [1783.247, 7.007], "Lanternhorses like that bridge. On some nights it glows there again. Look for it!": [1790.704, 4.895], "Champion! Before we fix the clock, we must set the right time on it.": [1796.049, 3.999], "Let me show you how to read a clock to five minutes. Then we\u2019ll fix it together!": [1800.497, 4.447], "The Canal Badge! Well done, {name}!": [1805.394, 1.737], "Quiz Night starts when you finish this chapter\u2019s lessons and help Rafi with his fish boxes. Come back then!": [1807.581, 6.559], "\u00a1Hola! I\u2019m Pedro, captain of the water taxis!": [1814.59, 2.825], "Stand by any yellow sign and press A. I\u2019ll take you anywhere in the city!": [1817.865, 4.468], "Later I\u2019ll teach you to read my canal map. When you see a ! over my head, come back. \u00a1Hasta luego!": [1822.783, 6.281], "Ahoy, {name}! I steer a water taxi now, with Pedro.": [1829.515, 2.911], "No more sneaking, just canals, boats and numbers. I love it!": [1832.875, 3.871], "Psst, {name}! Captain Jonah told me about his island fishing derby. Port Lumen has one too!": [1837.196, 5.556], "Catch two fish in the canals or the harbor, then tell me. We compare them. The longest goes on my board.": [1843.202, 6.473], "One derby a day. Ready, set, fish!": [1850.125, 2.313], "HELP WANTED. Board empty. Mayor Bea says: \"Notes soon! First learn to add and take away to 100 with Rafi.\"": [1852.889, 7.263], "HELP WANTED. You helped everyone today! New notes come every morning.": [1860.601, 4.127], "Tick-tock, {name}! I have two things for a number-line champion. What would you like?": [1865.178, 4.404], "Clock-hand jumps!. Learn to read a clock. Maybe later.": [1870.032, 3.209], "My big clock hands jump in tens! Want to help me count the jumps on a number line up to 100?": [1873.691, 6.303], "Yes, let\u2019s jump!. Maybe later.": [1880.444, 1.737], "Tick, tock, TEN! You jump in tens like a real clockmaker, {name}.": [1882.631, 3.743], "Can you keep a secret, {name}? Port Lumen has a magic creature!": [1886.824, 3.465], "On some nights, a little light glows in the Grand Canal. Look under the east bridge!": [1890.739, 5.044], "That is the Lanternhorse.": [1896.233, 1.46], "It only comes out at night, and only once in a while. See the glow? Cast your line right on it\u2026 be patient!": [1898.143, 6.516], "There is no hurry. It will still be there tomorrow night, or the next one.": [1905.109, 4.02], "Gus is right here, {name}. Say hello to him!": [1909.579, 2.313], "Then come and see me whenever you like. I'm in the Town Hall, up past the canal.": [1912.343, 4.703], "When the city is calm again, come and visit me! I'll be in the City Library, by the museums.": [1917.495, 5.663], "My hat shop is in the Galleria. Come and try on a hat when the clock is fixed!": [1923.608, 4.831], "Hello there! Say hello to our mayor first. She\u2019s right here!": [1928.889, 3.529], "Welcome to Port Lumen! I\u2019m Mayor Bea.": [1932.868, 2.441], "Since the storm, our big clock has stopped. Gus told me you came to help. Thank you, {name}!": [1935.759, 4.959], "Look at all the signs on Market Street! Some have words I bet you don\u2019t know yet. Shall we read them?": [1941.168, 5.769], "What a reader! Every sign on Market Street is clear now.": [1947.387, 3.316], "Oh no, oh no! My robot fell apart. Can you help me build something new with its pieces?": [1951.153, 5.471], "Beep boop! My new bridge works. Same pieces, new thing!": [1957.074, 3.38], "Ahoy, {name}! My harbor book needs a helper. What is moving in my harbor today?": [1960.904, 4.319], "My harbor book is shipshape. Fair winds, explorer!": [1965.673, 3.252]}}